---
name: vrchat-screenshot-metadata
description: Extract and interpret VRChat (VRCX) screenshot metadata from PNG iTXt chunks — world name, capture time, instance ID, player list, and convert VRChat IDs to profile/world URLs. Use when analyzing VRChat photos or building tooling around VRChat screenshot metadata.
---

# VRChat Screenshot Metadata Parser

## Overview

VRChat PCVR/Desktop screenshots are saved as PNG files with embedded metadata in PNG **iTXt chunks**, written by two sources:

- **VRChat client** — writes an XMP (Adobe XML/RDF) iTXt block under profile name `XML:com.adobe.xmp`
- **VRCX** (if installed) — appends a JSON iTXt block under profile name `Description`

On Windows, screenshots are saved to `%USERPROFILE%\Pictures\VRChat` by default, with optional `YYYY-MM` date subfolders (configurable via VRChat's `config.json` `picture_output_folder` / `picture_output_split_by_date`).

> Note: VRChat's XMP metadata was introduced in VRChat 2025.3.1+; older screenshots may only have VRCX JSON or no embedded metadata.

---

## XMP Block — `XML:com.adobe.xmp` (VRChat Native)

Namespaces:
- `xmp` → `http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/`
- `tiff` → `http://ns.adobe.com/tiff/1.0/`
- `dc` → `http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/`
- `vrc` → `http://ns.vrchat.com/vrc/1.0/`

| Field | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| `xmp:CreatorTool` | Always `VRChat` |
| `xmp:Author` | Display name of photographer |
| `xmp:CreateDate` | ISO 8601 timestamp, e.g. `2026-09-10T05:05:57.5564509+08:00` (7-digit sub-second = .NET DateTime ticks, 100ns precision) |
| `xmp:ModifyDate` | Same as CreateDate for screenshots |
| `tiff:DateTime` | Redundant copy of capture time |
| `dc:title` | Always empty |
| `vrc:WorldID` | `wrld_` + UUID (e.g. `wrld_91a35c65-3e14-4a01-85f3-8e34bb77ac2e`) |
| `vrc:WorldDisplayName` | Human-readable world name |
| `vrc:AuthorID` | `usr_` + UUID of photographer |

> Note: If the photo is taken in a **private/local world**, the WorldID and WorldDisplayName fields are **not** embedded.

---

## VRCX JSON Block — `Description` (VRCX)

json

{

"application": "VRCX",

"version": 1,

"author": { "id": "usr_...", "displayName": "..." },

"world": {

"name": "Cradle of Grass",

"id": "wrld_...",

"instanceId": "wrld...:56875~hidden(usr...)~region(jp)"

},

"players": [

{ "id": "usr_...", "displayName": "..." }

]

}


### Instance ID Format

{WorldID}:{InstanceNumber}~{AccessType}({HostUserID})~region({RegionCode})

- **AccessType**: `public`, `hidden`, `private`, `friends`, etc.
- **RegionCode**: `jp`, `usw`, `use`, `eu`, ...

---

## ID → URL Conversion

| ID Type | URL Pattern |
|---------|-------------|
| World ID (`wrld_...`) | `https://vrchat.com/home/world/{WorldID}/info` |
| User ID (`usr_...`) | `https://vrchat.com/home/user/{UserID}` |

Short link alternative for worlds: `https://vrch.at/{WorldID}` (redirects to the above)

---

## Parsing Notes / Pitfalls

- PNG iTXt text is **UTF-8** — decode display names as UTF-8, not Latin-1 (mis-decoding causes `å¸ƒè•¾èŒ¶èŒ¶`-style mojibake)
- `dc:title` is always present but empty
- XMP `CreateDate` uses `+08:00`-style offset, not `Z`
- VRCX JSON may be absent if VRCX was not running — fall back to XMP fields
- Player list includes **all users in instance** at capture moment, not just those in frame
- iTXt chunks appear after `IHDR` and before `IDAT`; scan all iTXt chunks by profile name


## Location
- Default on %userprofile%\Pictures
- If config.json exists, use it first.